    "body": "Merged #516's refreshed branch (rebuilt on #629's chuck-ward ladder), which brings main with it, to resolve conflicts.\n- **`cnc_thread.rs`:** main's required `HAND` and this PR's optional `ALT 1` are both kept, so the line is `... PULLOUT .. HAND .. [ALT 1]`. `CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` documents both.\n- **`thread_g76.nc` + `lathe_post_g76`:** #629's direction (start Z14 on the top centre, root at Z8, M03) with this PR's `R0.4` finishing depth.\n- **`thread_g76_area.nc` (regenerated):** only the direction changed. The flank record now starts at Z14.625 (top + D·tanθ) and ends at Z8, where it used to run Z7.375 → Z14. P, Q, R and the pass count are unchanged. `same_ladder`'s station check now reads `z0 - w·tanθ`, since the travel is -Z.\n- **Literals:** gained the other side's field.\n\nGate:\n- app: `lathe_post_g76` 8, `lathe_post_g76_schedule` 4, `lathe_post_refusals` 5, `lathe_post` 7, `inverted_post` 15, `turning_thread` 9, `turning_thread_infeed` 4, `conformance` 6, `posting` 17, `project_roundtrip` 71, `golden_cl` 23, lib 103.\n- post and motion thread suites: green.\n- clippy `-D warnings` on post (all targets) and app (lib + G76 tests): clean.\n\nStill a draft for a lathe run. Ready for a re-check (/resolve-conflicts check).",
